# Build context control.
#
# The image needs the service modules, the sync script, entrypoint.sh,
# templates/, static/, seed/ and tools/. Everything else in this directory is
# history, working notes or documentation, and shipping it wastes context
# transfer on every build. One entry matters for more than speed:
# app5.py still contains a hardcoded LAN IP, so keeping the dead versions out
# of the context keeps them out of any published layer too.

# Dead and superseded versions
app4.py
app5.py
app_old.py
app_old_*.py
app_pre_*.py
app_post_*.py
Dockerfile4
Dockerfile_old
extract_stream4.py
extract_stream_old.py

# Abandoned experiments
intercept_jw.py
test_stealth.py

# Verification harness, run against the built image rather than shipped in it.
# Every one is bind-mounted into a scratch container; none belongs in a layer.
tools/check_console.py
tools/check_render.py
tools/check_multiview.py
tools/check_ffmpeg.py
tools/check_reorder.py
tools/live_multiview_ui.py
_shots/

# Stale compose. The real one is the deployment's own.
docker-compose.yml

# Previous owner's snapshots
_backups/

# Documentation and working notes
*.md
docs/

# Agent tooling
.claude/

# Python and editor noise. The ** matters: a bare __pycache__/ matches only
# at the top of the context, and tools/__pycache__ was shipping.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore
